<newsitem itemid="190315" id="root" date="1996-11-14" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: SW Water H1 pretax profits rises.</title>
<headline>SW Water H1 pretax profits rises.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		 53.4		  vs  40.2</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	  11.8		  vs   9.8</p>
<p> Pretax			72.9		  vs  54.0</p>
<p> Turnover		   174.4		  vs 154.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 57 to 68 million stg.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 78.2		   vs 65.6</p>
<p> Bid response costs	4.9		   vs nil</p>
<p> Interest		    8.3		   vs 12.5</p>
<p> Tax			   4.7		   vs  3.0</p>
<p> Retained profit	  48.2		   vs 38.5</p>
<p> Pay date		   April 7, 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date  December 3</p>
<p> Ex-div date		November 25</p>
<p>Note - In October, the government blocked two proposed bids for South West Water, a water and sewerage company, from Severn Trent and Wessex Water.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
</text>
